course: dictionary
lesson: 5766
title: Lunar: words about the Moon
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lunar is an adjective, and it means to do with the Moon. When you meet it, ask yourself what the sentence is talking about, then read the words around it for clues.
explain: «In a lunar eclipse the Earth is between the Sun and the Moon.» The sentence names the Sun, the Earth and the Moon, so lunar must link to the Moon. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "In a Moon eclipse the Earth is between the Sun and the Moon" still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Lunar words show up in space, science and calendars. «Diwali, Eid, Hanukkah and Lunar New Year fall on different dates each year because they follow lunar or lunisolar calendars.» A lunar calendar follows the Moon, so its dates move from year to year.
fact: Lunar means to do with the Moon.
fact: A lunar month is about 29 and a half days, from one new moon to the next.
fact: A lunar eclipse is when the Earth's shadow falls on the Moon.
fact: Phrases to know: «lunar surface», «lunar landing», «lunar module» and «Lunar New Year».
fact: Apollo 11 was the first lunar landing that took astronauts to the Moon.
exercise: «In a lunar eclipse the Earth is between the Sun and the Moon.» What does lunar mean here? | To do with the Sun | *To do with the Moon | To do with the sea | To do with the stars
exercise: A lunar month is about how many days, from one new moon to the next? | 365 days | *29 and a half days | 7 days | 12 days
exercise: Which word means to do with the Moon? | *lunar | stellar | sunny | solar
test: «Diwali, Eid, Hanukkah and Lunar New Year fall on different dates each year.» Why do these dates change? | *They follow lunar or lunisolar calendars, which follow the Moon | They are always on the same date | They are chosen by the school | They follow the weather
test: What is a lunar eclipse? | A day when the Sun goes dark for a car | When the Moon falls onto the Earth | *When the Earth's shadow falls on the Moon | When a cloud covers a star
exam: Which word means to do with the Moon? | Polar | Oceanic | Solar | *Lunar
